kit/ppu_xforms -- the kit's PPU patch layer as AUTHORED transformations (Kit sem Python, Phase 2;
plan docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-26-gow2-kit-sem-python.md, format in ps3recomp tools/kit/xform.h).

ORDER             every recomp_mid_v2/patch_*.py, in ./apply_all_patches.sh --print-order order;
                  'noop <name>' = no effect on the pinned lift per the golden hash chain
                  (regenerate with kit/golden/xform_order.sh <scratch>; never edit the marks by hand).
RESIDUAL          effective ORDER names that still run as Python: '<name> TAB <reason>'.
                  'pending: ...' = not converted yet; any other reason = stays Python until the
                  lifter port (Phase 4). apply-xforms refuses an effective name that has neither
                  a .xform nor a RESIDUAL line.
<stem>.xform      patch <stem>.py as hash locators + text we wrote ('ps3kit-xform 1').
AUDIT_ALLOW.tsv   reviewed collisions for the template audit.

Controller ruling 1: nothing here may contain text taken from a lift. Locators are SHA-256 of
trimmed anchor lines; {{line}} and \1..\9 are the only ways lifted text reaches the output, at
apply time, from the user's own lift. Every .xform must pass
    ps3kit xform-audit kit/ppu_xforms <the user's raw lift>
(detection, not proof) AND the fragment review: every authored fragment, of any length, checked
against the patch script (text the script writes -- never its needle, never text only in the
lift), recorded per xform in the phase ledger, before it is committed.

Adding one (maintainer, scratch only -- never commit what the tools write):
    kit/golden/xform_convert.sh <ppu_raw> <scratch> <patch>.py     # draft + audit + fragments.tsv
    (review every fragments.tsv row against the patch script; copy the draft here)
    kit/golden/xform_check.sh   <ppu_raw> <scratch>                 # every ppu_after/* IDENTICAL
